            {
                "content": "# GILA RIVER BASIN (cont.)\n\nLocation.- In T. 3 N., R. 8 or 9 E., in the canyon, probably between sites of Etewart Mountain and Mormon Flat Dams, and about 15 miles upstream from Verde River.\n\nRecords available. - May to August 1890.\n\nDetermination of discharge. - Discharge computed by usual methods of stream gaging using gage heights, probably read daily on a staff gage, and current-meter discharge measurements.\n\nRemarks. - Records probably good; 21 discharge measurements were made during the 3-month period. Small diversions above station for irrigation. Record shows water avail- able from Salt River above Verde River for irrigation of Salt River Valley.\n\nMonthly summary of discharge of Salt River 50 miles above Phoenix, Ariz., 1890\n\n($ Corrected)\n\n<table><tr><th rowspan=\"2\">Month</th><th colspan=\"3\">Discharge in second-feet</th><th colspan=\"2\">Runoff</th></tr><tr><td>Maximum</td><td>Minimum</td><td>Mean</td><td>Second-\nfoot-days</td><td>Acre-feet</td></tr><tr><td>May 28 -31, 1890</td><td>520</td><td>520</td><td>520</td><td>-</td><td>14,130</td></tr><tr><td>June</td><td>520</td><td>193</td><td>298</td><td>-</td><td>17,730</td></tr><tr><td>July</td><td>375</td><td>185</td><td>215</td><td>-</td><td>13,220</td></tr><tr><td>August 1 -28</td><td>2,200</td><td>600</td><td>1,362</td><td>-</td><td>175,640</td></tr></table>",
